### Design Rationale Summary

| Decision | Reasoning |
|----------|-----------|
| **Rule type: `inventory_has`** | First choice per preference order — mine tasks produce inventory items. Spruce trapdoors always drop themselves when broken. |
| **Single rule** | One spruce_trapdoor in scene + zero in starting inventory = unambiguous completion signal. No additional spatial or event rules needed. |
| **No `position_inside_box`** | Task is "mine a block," not "navigate to a location." Position constraints would over-specify. |
| **No `count_in_box_at_most` for block removal** | While checking block removal at `~4,~1,~3` would work, it requires spawn-relative coordinate tracking and is more fragile than the inventory check. |
| **`min_count: 1`** | Exactly one trapdoor exists in the scene; mining it guarantees exactly 1 in inventory. |

